 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Empty Space Map Generation](1771-empty-space-map-generation.md)
-Empty Space Map Generation is a preprocessing technique that creates a boolean map indicating which voxels in a scalar field contain no visible geometry, allowing ray marching to skip empty regions. It reduces the number of density samples and transfer function evaluations by jumping over contiguous blocks of empty space. Unlike Distance Map Computation (Multi-Stage), which computes distances to occupied blocks, this method uses a binary occupancy check based on a transfer function threshold.
